            <ArticleTitle>Absolute quantification by droplet digital PCR versus analog real-time PCR.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1003-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/nmeth.2633</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nanoliter-sized droplet technology paired with digital PCR (ddPCR) holds promise for highly precise, absolute nucleic acid quantification. Our comparison of microRNA quantification by ddPCR and real-time PCR revealed greater precision (coefficients of variation decreased 37-86%) and improved day-to-day reproducibility (by a factor of seven) of ddPCR but with comparable sensitivity. When we applied ddPCR to serum microRNA biomarker analysis, this translated to superior diagnostic performance for identifying individuals with cancer.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
